# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. Never commit real credentials.
# Restart `npm run dev` after changing these — env vars are read at boot.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SMTP for the booking inquiry form (src/app/api/contact/route.ts).
#
# Without all three of HOST, USER and PASS the form refuses to send and tells
# the visitor to email or call instead. It will not silently drop inquiries.
#
# ── Using Gmail ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SMTP_PASS is NOT your Google password. It is a 16-character App Password:
#
#   1. Google Account → Security → turn on 2-Step Verification (required).
#   2. Google Account → Security → App passwords → generate one.
#   3. Paste it below with the spaces removed.
#
# Gmail will only send FROM the account that authenticates, which is why the
# email arrives from your own address. The visitor's address is set as
# Reply-To, so replying in your inbox answers them directly.
#
# Gmail's limit is roughly 500 messages/day — far beyond a venue's inquiries.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_USER=your-address@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your16charapppassword

# Where inquiries are delivered. Optional — defaults to VENUE.email in
# src/lib/content.ts, which is also the address printed on the site.
# CONTACT_TO=someone-else@example.com
